From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hal: size the encoder buffer on classic SoCs

The T10/T20 and other classic SDK encoders expect encAttr.bufSize to
describe the raw frame buffer. Leaving it at 0 makes the closed H264E
encoder dereference a NULL buffer in H264E_T10_SliceInit as soon as the
first frame is encoded, which segfaults the daemon right after the ISP
comes up.

Set it from the effective frame size, the same way prudynt does on
these platforms.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/src/hal/hal_ingenic.c
+++ b/src/hal/hal_ingenic.c
@@ -3315,7 +3315,9 @@
 #else
     a.encAttr.enType   = (v->codec==MS_VC_H265)?PT_H265:PT_H264;
 #endif
-    a.encAttr.bufSize  = 0;
+    /* Classic encoders size the raw frame buffer themselves; 0 leaves the
+     * H264E encoder with a NULL buffer when the first frame is encoded. */
+    a.encAttr.bufSize  = (uint32_t)(((ew * eh * 3 / 2) + 1023) & ~1023u);
     a.encAttr.profile  = v->profile;
     a.encAttr.picWidth = ew;
     a.encAttr.picHeight= eh;
